# Public Supabase settings for the browser build. Copy to .env.local (ignored by git) and fill in.
# These two values are PUBLIC: they are compiled into the site and visible to every visitor.
# NEVER put a service-role key, secret key (sb_secret_...), database password or any other privileged credential in a VITE_ variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Optional: 'supabase' (live data) or 'mock' (in-memory demo data, for local demos only).
# Unset: production builds use Supabase; local development uses Supabase when the two values above are set, else demo data.
# A production build never falls back to demo data on its own: if Supabase is misconfigured the site shows an error instead.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=
